Finance Tools — Equity Analyzer (v1.1)
A command‑line equity analysis engine that merges Yahoo Finance, Finviz, and custom rule‑based logic to generate a structured, multi‑factor evaluation of any stock.

This tool is designed for options strategy decision‑making, trend classification, and fundamental screening — all in one unified output.

🔍 What This Tool Does
When you run:

Code
￼
￼
Copy
./analyze TICKER
The system:

Fetches raw data from Yahoo Finance

Scrapes supplemental metrics from Finviz

Merges both sources into a unified JSON file

Applies rule‑based scoring across:

Balance sheet strength

Valuation

Growth

Profitability

Trend structure (SMA50/SMA200)

Options suitability (CSP, CC, Long Calls)

Prints a clean, color‑coded analysis to the terminal

Saves a full data snapshot as TICKER.json

🧠 Core Philosophy
This project is built on three principles:

1. No single metric is enough
True signal emerges only when fundamentals, trend, volatility, and sentiment are combined.

2. SMA and EMA are two schools of thought
Both are valid. SMA defines structure, EMA defines momentum.
The engine currently uses SMA50/SMA200 for structural trend — EMA momentum will be added in v1.2.

3. There is no end to better
The analyzer is intentionally modular so new layers can be added without breaking existing logic.

